### player-data-service — collection HTTP
#
# Requer a stack no ar:
#   docker compose -f infra/docker/docker-compose.yml up
#
# Todos os endpoints exigem um JWT do identity (ADR-0009). O login captura o token.
# GoLand/IntelliJ: clique no ▶. (VS Code REST Client: ver nota no fim.)
#
# Acompanhe: Grafana http://localhost:3000 e o banco em localhost:5434
# (db player_data, user/pass dev/dev).

@identityHost = http://localhost:8081
@playerDataHost = http://localhost:8083
@handle = Data_1
@password = supersecret

### (uma vez) Criar a conta no identity
POST {{identityHost}}/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "handle": "{{handle}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### Login no identity -> captura o token
# @name login
POST {{identityHost}}/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "handle": "{{handle}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

> {%
    client.global.set("token", response.body.token);
%}

### Gravar um valor (inventory/gold)
PUT {{playerDataHost}}/me/data/inventory/gold
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 100 }

### Gravar outro (inventory/potions)
PUT {{playerDataHost}}/me/data/inventory/potions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

5

### Ler um valor
GET {{playerDataHost}}/me/data/inventory/gold
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Ler o namespace inteiro -> { "gold": ..., "potions": ... }
GET {{playerDataHost}}/me/data/inventory
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Remover um valor (DELETE é idempotente)
DELETE {{playerDataHost}}/me/data/inventory/gold
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# --- VS Code REST Client ---
# O bloco "> {% ... %}" é sintaxe do HTTP Client do JetBrains. No REST Client,
# remova-o e use: Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
